<title>USA: EMERGENCY WEATHER CONDITIONS -  WSC - 30-JAN.</title>
<headline>EMERGENCY WEATHER CONDITIONS -  WSC - 30-JAN.</headline>
<text>
<p>Tropical cyclone Gretelle is now moving away from the South Africa coast. The system is becoming less of a risk to shipping as it continues to weaken. Top winds are now only 40 mph. The system should dissipate in about 36 hours.  </p>
<p>Tropical Cyclone Pancho-Helinda will threaten shipping over the open Indian Ocean. The storm has 50 mph top winds and is near 15s/91e, moving southwest.  </p>
<p>There are no further statements at this time.</p>
</text>
